<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ninlil</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ninlil was a Sumerian goddess, the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enlil">Enlil</a> and mother of the moon god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanna">Nanna</a>. Worshipped beside Enlil at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a>, she was identified with Sud, the patron goddess of Shuruppak. A Sumerian myth tells how Enlil was banished to the underworld for seizing her and how she followed him there. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> later identified her with the wife of Ashur.</p></div>
